next
  Summary: combat AI takeover, faction doctrines, flank and retreat behaviors, sniper aim mode, monolith combat, zombied shamble, danger rework, stealth kills, limp/heal fixes, AOEngine compatibility

  - Added Combat AI takeover on a configurable share of NPCs (slider, default 100%).
    Per-NPC stable hash decides which NPCs use AT combat vs. vanilla / modpack combat. Same NPC always lands the same side across save and load.
    Each NPC walks a list of allowed behaviors (chosen by community, HP, and weapon) every tick and picks the first one matching the current situation.
    Close-weapon carriers (pistol, shotgun, SMG, knife) charge the enemy. Low-HP NPCs retreat. Others advance through cover, take cover when exposed, fire from cover when peeking is possible, crouch and fire otherwise.
  - Added Combat AI takeover for monolith and zombied.
    Monolith use standard behavior selection by HP and weapon, same as other communities.
    Zombied walk toward the enemy firing, no cover seeking, no retreat.
  - Added per-faction combat doctrines.
    Military holds cover, snipes, flanks. Monolith charges with close weapons and never retreats.
    Bandits panic when hurt. Cowards flee outright. Mercs use military skillset but break under fire.
    Each NPC's doctrine is stable across save and load.
  - Added 3 combat behaviors. FLANKING goes around the enemy when line of sight is lost.
    RETREAT_AND_FIRE pulls back crouched while firing. FLEE sprints away with weapon strapped.
  - Added Sniper aim mode for kind=w_sniper carriers (SVD, SVT40, Mosin, SKS, M82 and the rest of the class).
    When a sniper has line of sight, they crouch and engage the engine sniper-aim flag, which tracks the target head direction instead of the weapon barrel direction. More precise aim at range.
  - Removed Stance Switch as a standalone system. Sniper crouching is now handled inside Combat for in-share NPCs and inherited from the vanilla planner for out-of-share NPCs.
  - Fixed Anomaly's xr_danger with a full-file script override and paired ltx.
    Hits, ricochets, and nearby gunshots each use their own config row (vanilla collapsed all three).
    Crashes near mutant bodies and stale animation across danger transitions are gone.
    Danger MCM tab: 3 toggles (combat_ignore override, gunshot disclosure, actor-source weighting).
  - Corpses stay dangerous for 15 minutes (was 12 seconds), ricochets for 10, weather affects range.
  - Added stealth-kill suppression to Hit Sharing (default on, MCM Stealth toggle).
    Silenced shots, scoped-rifle headshots, and backstabs no longer auto-disclose the shooter to the squad.
    Squadmates still learn through gunshot sound, corpse discovery, and line of sight.
  - Fixed limping animation to match the NPC's active weapon. NPCs with rifles, shotguns, or SMGs no longer get a fist-pose torso during the limp overlay.
  - Fixed NPCs staying stuck in a limp pose after their HP recovers. The looped animation now flushes when limp tracking ends.
  - Fixed healing NPCs not reacting to enemies. They now break the heal sequence when an enemy appears mid-clutch or mid-gesture.
  - Fixed crash on torn-down attacker reference during the attack-sound danger dispatch.
  - Fixed Combat AI silently turning off on NPCs that went offline and came back. AT combat now persists across offline cycles for the full lifetime of each NPC.
  - Fixed limping animation playing during combat. NPCs with an enemy in memory no longer limp. The cue is reserved for fully out-of-combat low-HP states.
  - Added AOEngine v0.55+ support.

1.0.0
  Summary: First release, hit sharing, NPC self-healing fix, per-rank accuracy, long-range rifle crouch
  First release. Four independent systems on top of one internal core. Full MCM configuration.
  Added: Hit Sharing - on first faction-enemy hit, force-disclose shooter to every online squadmate (force_set_goodwill, enable_memory_object, register_in_combat). Distant patrols and suppressor victims now engage on hit 1. Disclosure decays after the configured retention (default 2 game minutes of no further hits from that shooter), then re-fires on the next hit. New squad members inherit existing disclosures on spawn. Previously-offline shooters coming back online replay disclosure to every member of the squads tracking them.
  Added: NPC Self-Healing - DLTX overlay restores vanilla medkit and bandage item lists in xr_eat_medkit. Heal rate multiplier, per-rank healing-charge probability (novice, experienced, veteran, master), limping overlay, heal animation.
  Added: Accuracy - per-shot, per-rank NPC dispersion curve replacing the engine's broken rank curve. 8 per-tier dispersion sliders (novice 1.00 to legend 0.38).
  Added: Stance Switch - long-range rifle carriers (DMRs, battle rifles, bolt-actions: SVD, Mosin, SVT40, SKS, M82 and the rest of the kind=w_sniper LTX class) crouch when engine selects LookOut or HoldPosition. Crouch carries forward into KillEnemy, WaitInCover, HoldAmbushLocation through body_state inheritance.
  Added: MCM reset-to-defaults button (Development tab).
  Added: console test commands at_spawn, at_spawn_veteran, at_spawn_master, at_spawn_far, at_dump.
